/E (Like sanitation infrastructure, vaccination, and modern epidemiologic surveillance before it, AI represents a systems-level shift with the potential to fundamentally alter public health practice. But unlike prior technological transitions, the pace, scale, and uncertainty surrounding AI are unprecedented. The public health community is confronting a rapidly evolving landscape in which AI is being adopted faster than governance structures, educational models, and workforce readiness efforts can keep pace.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
