<<
/Title (If used responsibly, AI can strengthen disease surveillance, improve emergency preparedness, accelerate research and discovery, communicate more effectively and help identify life-saving patterns through integrated clinical-, genomic-, and SDoH-informed care. Conversely, if used without care or without public health expertise at the table, it risks reinforcing historical bias, widening existing inequities and eroding community trust.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2128 0 R
>>
